  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Solve these trigonometric equations for $x\\in[0,2\\pi)$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin x=\\cos x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac\\pi4,\\frac{5\\pi}4$",
          "worked": "When $\\cos x=0$, the original equation is not satisfied. Divide by $\\cos x$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\tan x&=1\\\\x&=\\frac\\pi4,\\frac{5\\pi}4\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt3\\sin x=\\cos x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac\\pi6,\\frac{7\\pi}6$",
          "worked": "When $\\cos x=0$, the original equation is not satisfied. Divide by $\\cos x$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt3\\tan x&=1\\\\\\tan x&=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\\\x&=\\frac\\pi6,\\frac{7\\pi}6\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\sin x+\\cos x=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{3\\pi}4,\\frac{7\\pi}4$",
          "worked": "When $\\cos x=0$, the original equation is not satisfied. Divide by $\\cos x$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\tan x+1&=0\\\\\\tan x&=-1\\\\x&=\\frac{3\\pi}4,\\frac{7\\pi}4\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sin 2x=\\cos 2x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac\\pi8,\\frac{5\\pi}8,\\frac{9\\pi}8,\\frac{13\\pi}8$",
          "worked": "Let $u=2x$, so $0\\le u<4\\pi$. When $\\cos u=0$, the original equation is not satisfied. Divide by $\\cos u$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\tan u&=1\\\\u&=\\frac\\pi4,\\frac{5\\pi}4,\\frac{9\\pi}4,\\frac{13\\pi}4\\\\x&=\\frac\\pi8,\\frac{5\\pi}8,\\frac{9\\pi}8,\\frac{13\\pi}8\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      }
    ]
  },
